  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Fifty-Five (Irish trick-taking auction). Setup: 3-6 players, standard 52-card deck. Each player dealt 5 cards. Bidding phase: players bid in multiples of 5 (5-30). Highest bidder chooses trump and leads. Card rankings: Trumps (5 high, Jack, Ace of Hearts, Ace of trump, K). Red non-trump: K-A (A low). Black non-trump: K-J-A (A high). Ace of Hearts always trump. Gameplay: 5 tricks. Follow suit if able. Scoring: 5 points per trick. Jinking: bidder winning first 3 tricks can jink (go for all 5) for 25 points (lose all if fail).',
    Player: "Welcome to Fifty-Five, where Irish tradition meets high-stakes card play. Master the unique rankings: in red suits, Aces are low; in black suits, Aces are high. The Five of Trumps is the strongest card in the game. The Ace of Hearts is always trump. Bid smartly, lead strategically, and watch for the 'jink' opportunity to double your points.",
    objective: 'Be the first player or team to reach 55 points. Points are scored primarily by winning tricks (5 points per trick).',
    gameplay: "1. Lead: The highest bidder leads the first card.\n2. Trumping: You are NEVER forced to play a trump unless a HIGHER trump is led. You may play a trump even if you can follow suit.\n3. Robbing: If the turnndup card (the trump marker) is an Ace, the dealer can 'rob' it by swapping a low card for it.",
    keyRules: [
      "Jinking: If a player wins the first 3 tricks and feels they can win all 5, they may 'jink' to win bonus points. If they lose any remaining trick, they lose all points for that hand.",
      'Ace of Hearts: Always the 3rd best card in the game, regardless of the suit called.',
      "Reneging: A specialized rule where high trumps don't have to follow lower ones.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
